341|v|To move to action; to actuate; to animate. ; To perform; to execute; to do. ; To perform, as an actor; to represent dramatically on the stage. ; To assume the office or character of; to play; to personate; as, to act the hero. ; To feign or counterfeit; to simulate. ; To exert power; to produce an effect; as, the stomach acts upon food. ; To perform actions; to fulfill functions; to put forth energy; to move, as opposed to remaining at rest; to carry into effect a determination of the will. ; To behave or conduct, as in morals, private duties, or public offices; to bear or deport one's self; as, we know not why he has acted so. ; To perform on the stage; to represent a character.	o:8gky,97,10;a5ih,52,3;g6w,51,2;8s0d,50,2;9uwe,42,3;1uta,41,2;2mj9,36,46;8spb,35,3;1q5z,34,5;9t86,33,1;4m9l,30,10;a7ot,30,4;6sai,28,13;3stf,28,6;a5oj,23,36~9s0f,16,214;2mj9,36,46;a5oj,23,36;6sai,28,13;4m9l,30,10;8gky,97,10;9mf,10,8;3stf,28,6;1q5z,34,5;a7ot,30,4;9uwe,42,3;6w6v,0,3;5ukh,3,3;8spb,35,3;alrc,12,3	s:69mc,86,7;ad4u,72,4;69nz,63,17;6wsb,58,12;23lo,57,5;3re,53,8;a2mm,52,20;7x5j,50,1;6x8n,50,37;9r39,50,33;3n1m,49,20;7hnp,48,2;9t1i,45,10;3ek8,45,1073;8b66,45,43~3ek8,45,1073;70j5,4,800;6ojf,40,767;3vm1,15,344;9t5i,40,291;14ax,17,197;5m8c,16,187;19jr,34,136;2c92,19,112;5wua,23,112;6x8z,14,112;7yx0,23,89;3bc,1,79;47h1,14,78;71i4,19,73	d:ae8g,56,6;555z,40,7;a2c9,35,14;1x5z,31,3;1nij,29,20;8duo,27,14;76mq,26,6;2rv7,25,284;aejw,24,10;ak2w,24,3;5oeb,24,11;1scs,23,9;7f3i,22,3;82bt,21,6;1qof,20,9~b90,8,1133;snc,8,441;6l12,3,335;304t,17,328;2rv7,25,284;8us9,4,281;6886,3,132;1nij,29,20;a2c9,35,14;8duo,27,14;5oeb,24,11;aejw,24,10;1scs,23,9;1qof,20,9;555z,40,7	D:4d3z,98,30;adbe,93,16;2z0p,93,12;1z78,92,4;1vw1,90,22;a1pz,90,46;6c8o,90,13;5mk7,89,11;v6f,89,10;4lyr,89,15;b5l,88,11;8gky,87,5;6efl,87,129;9tar,86,692;1wwl,86,10~2fn3,59,2371;248,65,1627;31xy,8,781;9tar,86,692;4fdk,52,660;9v3i,58,653;3grl,49,431;6esa,18,391;8oyc,25,368;7h2o,14,354;7nk2,22,334;hb2,46,280;8utr,13,199;4d0i,8,168;947c,4